==================================================================
DAY 38 - PART A: THEORY
Building a Real Cluster with kubeadm, Part 1: Prerequisites
Time: 40 minutes
==================================================================

1. WHY DO THIS?
---------------
kind hides the setup. Building with kubeadm on real VMs teaches what
every node needs and is required knowledge for the CKA exam and for
on-premises clusters.


2. LAB DESIGN
-------------
  cp1      control plane   2 vCPU, 2-4 GB RAM, 20 GB disk
  worker1  worker          2 vCPU, 2 GB RAM
  worker2  worker          2 vCPU, 2 GB RAM
All on one network that can reach each other and the internet.
Options: VirtualBox/VMware/KVM VMs, Multipass (Ubuntu), or 3 small
cloud VMs. Use the same OS on all (Rocky/RHEL 9 or Ubuntu 22.04/24.04).


3. WHAT EVERY NODE NEEDS
------------------------
  - unique hostname, MAC, product_uuid
  - swap OFF (or explicitly configured; simplest is off)
  - kernel modules: overlay, br_netfilter
  - sysctls: net.bridge.bridge-nf-call-iptables=1,
             net.ipv4.ip_forward=1
  - a container runtime: containerd, with SystemdCgroup = true
    (kubelet and runtime must use the SAME cgroup driver: systemd)
  - kubelet, kubeadm, kubectl from pkgs.k8s.io, same versions
  - ports open:
      control plane: 6443 (API), 2379-2380 (etcd), 10250 (kubelet),
                     10257, 10259
      workers:       10250, 30000-32767 (NodePorts)
      plus your CNI's ports (Calico: 179 BGP, 4789 VXLAN, 5473 Typha)
  - RHEL family: SELinux permissive for the lab, firewalld rules or off


4. WHAT EACH PACKAGE DOES
-------------------------
  kubeadm   bootstraps the cluster (certs, kubeconfigs, static pods,
            join tokens). Runs once per node, then for upgrades.
  kubelet   systemd service on every node; runs pods.
  kubectl   client.
  containerd + runc   runtime.
  crictl    CLI for the runtime (CRI); like docker ps for Kubernetes.


5. VERSIONS
-----------
Kubernetes releases a minor version about every 4 months; each is
supported ~14 months. kubeadm, kubelet and kubectl are pinned and
held (not auto-updated) because upgrades must be done in order, one
minor version at a time (Day 40).


KEY POINTS TO REMEMBER
----------------------
- Swap off, modules + sysctls, containerd with systemd cgroups.
- Install and HOLD kubeadm/kubelet/kubectl.
- Open the required ports.
